             {:verdict
              "the chair's discipline is better than its spelling, and its semantics are better than both - everywhere a DECISION was required tw made the right one (Ps 22:17 keeps the kethib 'se ogyata no' where every commercial Bible reads pierced; Isa 7:14 declines the virgin-technical term for obaabunu; Gen 22:8 stands bare with no atonement doctrine put in Abraham's mouth, the exact place ff had to be walked back; Dan 3:12 keeps its negation; Ex 3:14 transliterates Ehyeh dee Ehyeh), and TWICE it told apart words the Hebrew spells identically - שאול is both Saul and Sheol across 468 seats with NOT ONE CROSSING, and it uses Seol never asaman; צבאות is hosts, gazelles and the women who served, and the chair had all three right while scattering the title across 64 spellings. What failed was never judgment but consistency; discharged",
              :headline
              "SEVEN VERSES WERE NOT IN TWI AT ALL - the press fell back to the en floor wholesale, in consecutive runs (Ps 53:5-7, Ruth 1:13-16), and Ruth 1:16 is her vow, one of the most quoted sentences in the Bible, sitting in English inside a Twi Bible. No count-based gate can see this; only a thermometer can, and only with a whitelist - a first sweep without one flagged 7,931 verses because the word list held 'a', 'do', 'be' and 'we', every one of them a common Twi word",
