             :cruxes
             ["THE ROOT WOUND WAS ONE WOUND IN FOUR COSTUMES: the floor uses angle brackets for TWO jobs - the את marker and the supplied word English needs where the Hebrew writes nothing - and the chair learned the shape and lost the distinction. It produced 706 English words left untranslated inside brackets, 595 of 598 fabricated markers (1 Chr 13:6 writes ⟨את⟩ where the floor writes ⟨the Name⟩), most of the 23 marker verses left for a reader, and the wrapper class ⟨⟨את⟩ asase⟩ - a supplied bracket thrown around a marker AND ITS OBJECT. ff left zero English in a bracket off the same floor; the standard was always reachable"
              "A FABRICATED MARKER HID BEHIND A MISSPELT BRACKET: Ex 29:22 carried a seventh ⟨את⟩ written with a U+3015 tortoise-shell close, invisible to every counter in the groove while the floor and the token row both said six. Bracket-glyph drift is documented fleet behaviour (ff found it too); here it concealed a fabrication"
              "THE CHAIR CORRECTED ITSELF IN THE DATA AND HEDGED: thirteen erasure seats carry BOTH words in one gloss - 'Eloohim (Onyankopon)', 'Onyankopon - Eloohim', 'ne Onyame (Eloohim)' - and Ezra 6:22 does it in the flow. The press knew the rail and set the old word down beside it"
              "THE HEBREW STOOD IN FRONT OF ITS OWN ANSWER: at Esther 7:9 העץ - Haman's gallows - leaked out of the token row into the flow inside an unclosed bracket, standing before its own correct gloss 'dua no'; the same shape at ⟨התו⟩ nkyerɛnne no (Ezek 9:6, the mark) and ⟨הנני⟩ (hwɛ, me wo ha)"
              "DRAFT-SPEAK REACHED THE CENTRE VERSE: Lev 8:35, the verse the whole 4D space folds onto, read '⟨את⟩ nhyɛnwee (guard duty) no so' - an English stage direction in the Torah's centre. Five such parentheticals stripped; two LEFT deliberately (Isa 19:19, where removing it would hide a mistranslation, and Gen 50:2, where the parenthesis holds Hebrew)"
              "THE NAME FAILED TWICE IN 6,943 SEATS: Isa 12:4 read 'Yawhɛ', the Name misspelt in the verse that says call on his name; Lev 7:20 had an EMPTY gloss at ליהוה while its flow carried the Name twice. A word count of Yawe returns 6,943 and calls it done - only a seat-by-seat sweep against the floor finds these"
              "ONE OF MY OWN REPAIRS BROKE A VERSE AND IDEMPOTENCE CAUGHT IT: the unbalanced-bracket rule ⟩x⟩ -> ⟨x⟩ reached across an intact marker at Gen 1:25 and took it apart. The delimiter-strip guarantee PASSED - no word was swallowed, the delimiters had merely moved THROUGH a marker. What caught it was a later pass reporting work on an already-repaired corpus. Markers are now parked behind a sentinel during rebalancing: untouchable by construction, not by luck"
              "THE POLYSEMY GUARD IS THE FLOOR, NEVER THE SPELLING: צבאות is the divine title, the GAZELLES of Song 2:7 and 3:5, and the WOMEN WHO SERVED at 1 Sam 2:22 - the chair had all three right and a spelling sweep would have made them all the LORD of Hosts. Same discipline kept Dagon's epithet out of the erasure cure at 1 Sam 5:7, and kept Saul out of Sheol at 468 seats"
              "THE RESIDUE CAME IN PAIRS: 37 of the burn's 42 gaps were exactly two consecutive verses - the relay's batch grain showing through the holes. The same grain shaped the zero-token clusters (2 Chr 5:1-4, 2 Sam 13:33-36) and the English fallbacks (Ps 53:5-7, Ruth 1:13-16)"
